From b029554e34cb6338c96d6e1c9d2e6ab1a78d61e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivy Evans <ivy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:06:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Controller: the left stick navigates the screens that
 navigate themselves

In character generation the D-pad moved the selection and the left
stick did nothing. On a screen the engine navigates itself, the D-pad
sends the retained direction codes and the focus layer stands down
("the engine routes it itself"); the stick only ever reached the focus
layer, so its press was dropped there.

Extend the dialogue fold to the GUI class, all four directions: the
stick's latched direction is folded into the button word before the
D-pad loop, so it takes the D-pad's path exactly, the engine's codes
where the engine owns the axis and the focus layer where KMRP does,
with the same press, release and hold-repeat. A folded direction is not
the D-pad to the gameplay HUD: character generation has no HUD to
consume the request, which would otherwise wait and move the action bar
on the first gameplay frame.
